# tools/cr/crypto_kumara_path_witness.rish -- the Kumara identity path authored in pure Rye, authoring NO new cryptography. The identity arc's
# account-path rung, the ed25519 sibling of crypto/bip44.rye: where crypto/slip10_ed25519.rye grows a whole tree of ed25519 identity keys and
# derives a child by a bare hardened index, this rung is the CONVENTION that gives that tree its named shape m/44'/coin_type'/account'/index' --
# every level hardened, since ed25519/SLIP-0010 has no watch-only public-parent path -- so a keeper's Kumara identity is reached the same way from
# the same phrase on any device. parse_path reads the human path text into the exact 32-bit hardened index list (a bare index refused
# NotHardened); derive_path and derive_identity walk crypto/slip10_ed25519.rye's ckd_priv down it (crypto - Season G).
#
# Season: crypto -- Season G (the Six-Season double-seat). This rung contributes only the path grammar over the already-GREEN
# crypto/slip10_ed25519.rye, itself only HMAC-SHA-512 and the ed25519 public derivation, both proven byte-for-byte on metal. Design read:
# active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md (Season G - the crypto parity wave).
# Clean-room: the BIP-44 path convention and SLIP-0010's ed25519 test vectors are public standards; the parser and walk are ours, standing on our
# own parity-GREEN SLIP-0010 derivation, never a copied line (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# Parity is proven at selftest the replayable way the tree favours, against SLIP-0010's OWN published ed25519 test vectors (the spec's own
# known-answers, quoted character for character from the canonical satoshilabs/slips slip-0010.md, never fabricated): all six nodes of BOTH Test
# Vector 1 (seed 000102...0f) and Test Vector 2 (the 64-byte seed), each walked BY ITS HUMAN PATH STRING ("m" ... "m/0'/1'/2'/2'/1000000000'"),
# reproduce EXACTLY the spec's published private key, chain code, AND 33-byte public key -- proving the parser, the hardening requirement, and the
# walk together against a real standard answer. The Kumara convention m/44'/0'/0'/0' parses to the exact all-hardened index list, derive_identity
# and derive_path agree byte-for-byte, and a malformed path (a bare non-hardened index, no master, a non-digit index, an index at 2³¹, a too-deep
# path, a trailing slash) each raises its named error. Purely local -- every key is a TEST key from the spec's own seeds, no network, no funds;
# growing a real Kumara identity and signing with its key stays the custody gate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cr/crypto_kumara_path_witness.rish

say "crypto-kumara-path: Language EN — the Kumara identity path: the identity arc's account-path rung, the ed25519 sibling of crypto/bip44.rye. Where crypto/slip10_ed25519.rye grows a tree of ed25519 identity keys, this rung is the CONVENTION that gives it the named shape m/44'/coin_type'/account'/index', every level hardened because ed25519 has no watch-only public-parent path, so a keeper's Kumara identity is reached the same way from the same phrase on any device. parse_path reads the human path text into the exact 32-bit hardened index list; derive_path and derive_identity walk slip10's ckd_priv. Authors no new cryptography — every byte is the GREEN crypto/slip10_ed25519.rye derivation beneath."
say "crypto-kumara-path: Style Radiant — one backup phrase and one named path, and a keeper's Kumara signing identity stands the same on every device that reads it. The wallet arc's account-path convention turned toward Grain's own identity, authored in the open and proven against the standard's own answers."
say "crypto-kumara-path: Lens TAME — every width named (a 32-bit index list bounded at sixteen levels, ten-digit decimal tokens, the hardened offset added by the parser itself), contract asserts on the master root, the parsed depth, and each walk step; it calls no cryptography of its own, only the GREEN crypto/slip10_ed25519.rye beneath. Parity holds against SLIP-0010's OWN published ed25519 test vectors 1 and 2: all six nodes of each, walked BY HUMAN PATH STRING, reproduce EXACTLY the spec's private key, chain code, and 0x00-prefixed public key. derive_identity and derive_path agree byte-for-byte; a bare non-hardened index refuses NotHardened, and every malformed path raises its named error. Purely local — TEST keys only, no real identity key, no network, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "crypto/bin/kumara_path"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build crypto/kumara_path.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "crypto-kumara-path: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "crypto/bin/kumara_path.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "crypto-kumara-path: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "crypto-kumara-path: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN crypto-kumara-path' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "crypto-kumara-path: selftest did not print the GREEN crypto-kumara-path line"
